<title>USA: U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef steady to weak on light to moderate demand and moderate offerings.  Select and Choice rib and round cuts weak, while loin cuts generally steady and chuck cuts uneven.  Beef trimmings steady to weak on light demand. - USDA</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>259 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 11 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>35 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     103.44	102.84	 96.41	 95.70</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.12	 -0.34	 -0.23	 -0.12</p>
<p>Rib	  163.80	163.67	144.67	143.79</p>
<p>Chuck	 71.66	 70.67	 72.44	 71.06</p>
<p>Round	 90.32	 90.32	 87.67	 87.67</p>
<p>Loin	 162.21	160.82	140.27	139.38</p>
<p>Brisket     58.11	 58.11	 60.00	 60.00</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  64.10	 64.03	 64.34	 64.17</p>
<p>Flank	 58.51	 58.51	 57.66	 57.66</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
